# NYC Crime Data Analysis (BigQuery & SQL)

This project explores and analyzes New York City crime data using **Google BigQuery**. It focuses on identifying high-risk areas, the most common types of crimes, and historical crime trends to provide data-driven insights.

## 📊 Project Overview
The analysis is performed on the `nyc_crime_dataset` hosted on Google Cloud Platform. By utilizing SQL (GoogleSQL), I extracted key metrics to understand the safety landscape of various NYC boroughs and areas.

## 🔍 Key Insights & Queries

#Preview Data

SELECT *
FROM `booming-octane-374400.nyc_crime_dataset.crime_data`
LIMIT 1000;

#Top 5 Crime Types
SELECT Crm_Cd_Desc, COUNT(*) AS total
FROM `booming-octane-374400.nyc_crime_dataset.crime_data`
GROUP BY Crm_Cd_Desc
ORDER BY total DESC
LIMIT 5;

#Crimes per Borough
SELECT AREA_NAME, COUNT(*) AS total
FROM `booming-octane-374400.nyc_crime_dataset.crime_data`
GROUP BY AREA_NAME
ORDER BY total DESC;

#Crime Trends Over Years
SELECT 'Column "date" not found in schema' AS error_info, *
FROM `booming-octane-374400.nyc_crime_dataset.crime_data`
LIMIT 10; 

#Views or Summary Tables CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE `booming-octane-374400.nyc_crime_dataset.top_crimes_summary` AS
SELECT Crm_Cd_Desc, COUNT(*) AS total
FROM `booming-octane-374400.nyc_crime_dataset.crime_data`
GROUP BY Crm_Cd_Desc
ORDER BY total DESC;

#Visualize High-Risk Areas
SELECT AREA_NAME, SUM(Count) AS total
FROM `booming-octane-374400.nyc_crime_dataset.crime_data`
GROUP BY AREA_NAME
ORDER BY total DESC;


